  "per_trial_wall_seconds": 120,
  "purpose": "Six frozen truth-aligned raw-bit receiver captures: bits 0 and 1 paired under identical key/oscillator seed 62013 and additive-noise seed 72013 at path scales 0, 0.5 and 1, with effect seeds 62031, 62032 and 62033 respectively. Keep the HF Worst / Each 65% / Margin 3 tight-arrival clock-edge profile, reference waveform, C/N0 43 dB-Hz and requested 2-second DATA fixture override; report actual prepared bit length and calendar from the receipt. Each row emits six contiguous DATA slots followed by two physical quiet apertures, is capped at 1.2M samples / 120 seconds, and scores truth-aligned raw-bit outcomes. Report decision types, first correct ordinal/time, longest no-correct run, final quiet completion, full-calendar elapsed time and source/channel/key fingerprints independently of codec output. These six correlated paired captures and their 36 active apertures are not independent trials, a population success rate, or a capacity qualification. Conditional follow-up only if any primary row has wrong, ambiguous or active-quiet DATA: at most one matched thermal-off capture per bit for the highest path scale with such errors (severity order 1 > 0.5 > 0; manifest order breaks ties); retain the same oscillator, additive-noise, path and key seeds and preserve positive receiver noise. No seed replacement or budget expansion.",
  "schema_version": 1
}
